<p><strong>Date basis:</strong> {{ $report['date_basis'] }}. Reporting period: {{ $report['period'] }}. Date ranges are inclusive and use Africa/Johannesburg. The additional deadline range ({{ $report['deadline_period'] }}) and overdue filter ({{ $report['overdue_status'] }}) narrow the same cohort on screen, in PDF and in Excel. Unknown historical dates are excluded when filtering by that date.</p>
<p style="margin-top:8px"><strong>Still overdue:</strong> Assigned or In progress after its deadline, measured as of {{ $report['generated_at'] }} SAST. <strong>Completed late:</strong> currently Completed with a known completion time strictly after its deadline. Completing exactly at the deadline is on time. Completed-late time stops at completion; review time has no effect. The report deadline uses the current completion attempt's retained deadline where available, otherwise the task deadline. The original date-basis option “Tasks due in period” continues to use the current task deadline.</p>
<p style="margin-top:8px"><strong>First-completion on-time rate:</strong> on-time first completions / non-cancelled tasks with at least one recorded completion attempt. Each attempt keeps its original deadline. Latest punctuality uses the latest completion attempt. These historical metrics are separate from the current Completed-late total.</p>
<p style="margin-top:8px"><strong>Completed:</strong> tasks currently Completed. Reviewed and Not reviewed are separate counts within Completed. <strong>Open:</strong> Assigned or In progress. Reopened work returns to Assigned and needs a new completion; previous attempts remain in history. Cancelled tasks are excluded from both overdue totals and punctuality denominators. Each saved recurring occurrence has its own status and deadline and is counted separately; future calendar previews are not task records. Corrections count historical returned attempts and reopening events.</p>
<p style="margin-top:8px">Categories and priorities provide context. Task counts are not a complete productivity score. Elapsed time is not hours worked. A missing historical completion time is shown as unknown and is not counted as completed late.</p>
